<p>The converse direction (Theorem 2) is validated by sweeping the generalized normal family with shape parameter α: R² peaks sharply at α=2 (Gaussian) and degrades for all other distributions. SIGReg maintains a wider plateau than VICReg for heavy-tailed latents, consistent with its more aggressive Gaussianization.</p>
</section>

<!-- ─── §06 PLANNING ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="s-planning" data-code="planning">
<div class="section-no">06 — Planning</div>
<h2>Identifiable Representations Enable Optimal Planning</h2>

<p>What does linear identifiability buy for downstream use? Theorem 4 provides the answer: if the cost function is invariant to orthogonal transformations (as is the case for distance-based costs like goal-reaching), then planning in the learned latent space is <em>mathematically identical</em> to planning in the true world. The optimal actions and value function transfer without modification.</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">Theorem 4 — Optimal Latent Planning</div>
  If h(z) = Qz (Q orthogonal) and costs ℓ are O(n)-invariant:<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;V̂*(h(z₀)) = V*(z₀) &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="math-comment">← same optimal value</span><br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;â*₁:T(h(z₀)) = a*₁:T(z₀) &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="math-comment">← same optimal actions</span>
</div>

<p>The paper tests this on the DMC Reacher task, where the true latent is a 2D joint angle (θ₀, θ₁). Two training conditions are compared: (1) <strong>OU pairs</strong> — samples drawn i.i.d. from the Gaussian world (high identifiability), and (2) <strong>RL trajectory pairs</strong> — consecutive frames from a goal-directed policy (non-Gaussian marginals, breaks theory assumptions).</p>

<!-- Planning results visualization -->
<div class="vp" id="s-planning-viz">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">latent-space planning — control cost vs encoder quality</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">lower cost = better planning</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <p style="font-size:.72rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.75rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono)">Control cost over 30 random start-goal pairs (path length ≥ 1; ideal = 1.0)</p>
    <div class="results-bars" id="planning-bars">
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label" style="color:var(--muted)">Oracle (ground truth)</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="26" style="background:rgba(16,185,129,.7)"><span>1.04</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label" style="color:var(--purple-l)">OU encoder (R²=0.95)</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="28" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,.7)"><span>1.11</span></div></div>
      </div>
